# Context Menu System Implementation Checklist

Status: Phase 4 complete; interactive presentation not started

## Goal

Add a reusable DwarfUI context-menu system whose registration and target
resolution resemble the existing tooltip system while providing synchronous
right-click ownership and an interactive menu.

A caller registers a small `ContextMenuDefinition` against either a UI widget
or an exact map tile. Right-clicking an eligible registered target opens one
menu and consumes the complete actionable right-click input event. UI-widget
menus are anchored to the captured screen position. Map-tile menus retain their
world position and are reprojected before every render so they remain attached
while the map viewport moves.

## Locked product decisions

- [ ] All context-menu-owned production modules live under
      `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/context_menu/`.
- [ ] All focused unit and DwarfSpec files live under
      `tests/context_menu/`.
- [ ] The public facade is loaded with
      `reqscript('dwarfui/context_menu/api')`; do not add a top-level
      `dwarfui/context_menu.lua` compatibility facade.
- [ ] A UI-widget registration opens at the screen position captured from the
      opening right-click.
- [ ] A map-tile registration opens from an exact world tile and recomputes
      its projected screen position before every render.
- [ ] "Screen position" means the DFHack screen/interface coordinate space
      used by widget frames, mouse input, and interface painting. It does not
      mean an operating-system physical display pixel.
- [ ] Screen-position anchors remain fixed for the open session, apart from
      menu-frame reclamping after an interface-size change.
- [ ] The preferred menu frame starts with its top-left cell at the captured
      or projected anchor. If that frame overflows, place the menu to the left
      and/or above the anchor before applying final screen-edge clamping.
- [ ] Map placement uses the canonical interface cell returned by the shared
      world-to-interface projection for the exact registered tile. It does not
      invent a separate tile-center or physical-pixel coordinate.
- [ ] Map-tile anchors move with camera panning and zoom and close when the
      source tile is no longer projectable on the displayed z-level or inside
      the visible map viewport.
- [ ] Opening occurs on the actionable `_MOUSE_R` event. When that event
      resolves a registered target, consume the complete input table so native
      DF and other UI cannot also react. Any additional keys in that table are
      consumed with the opening event.
- [ ] The initial design has no mouse-down latch or post-dismissal trailing
      boundary suppression. `_MOUSE_R_DOWN` and `_MOUSE_L_DOWN` alone are not
      opening, dismissal, or selection events. Phase 0 must verify this against
      the active DFHack input seams before implementation proceeds.
- [ ] `LEAVESCREEN`/Escape closes the open menu and consumes the complete input
      table containing that key.
- [ ] A second actionable `_MOUSE_R` closes the open menu, consumes its complete
      input table, and does not reopen another target.
- [ ] Left-clicking an entry closes the menu, consumes the input, and invokes
      that entry exactly once.
- [ ] Left-clicking outside the menu on actionable `_MOUSE_L` closes it and
      consumes the complete input table.
- [ ] Selecting an entry by keyboard also closes before invoking its handler
      and consumes the complete selection input table.
- [ ] The definition used by an open menu is a validated snapshot. Updating a
      registration affects its next opening, not the current session.
- [ ] Snapshot isolation applies to definition table structure and field
      values. An `on_select` function retains ordinary Lua closure semantics
      for any external state captured by that function.
- [ ] Entry colors resolve independently in this order: entry override,
      menu-level default, system default.
- [ ] Every `fg` and `bg` value is an integer display color in the inclusive
      `COLOR_BLACK` through `COLOR_WHITE` domain (`0..15`); `COLOR_RESET`,
      pens, strings, callable values, and out-of-domain integers are rejected.
- [ ] The initial system uses `COLOR_WHITE` as the system foreground default
      and `COLOR_BLACK` as the system background default.
- [ ] The resolved menu-level foreground/background pen colors the Window
      frame, optional native title, and otherwise-unpainted body. Entry rows use
      their independently resolved pens. Build a per-menu frame style without
      mutating `gui.FRAME_INTERIOR` or any other shared style table.
- [ ] UI-widget targets take precedence over map-tile targets. A blocking
      DwarfUI widget region suppresses map fallback within the traversed
      DwarfUI root even when that region has no context menu.
- [ ] Within one DwarfUI root, reverse render order determines the hit result.
      Across multiple eligible DwarfUI roots, the registered widget with the
      latest original registration sequence wins, matching the tooltip target
      detector. Re-registering the same widget does not change that sequence.
- [ ] A registered widget target found in any eligible root wins over blockers
      in other roots. If no registered widget target is found, a blocker in any
      traversed eligible root suppresses map fallback.
- [ ] A map registration is eligible only while its weak owner resolves through
      the shared root resolver to a visible, active, enabled root in the
      currently presented parent/root chain. Reevaluate that owner root for
      every opening sample and open-session validation.
- [ ] The menu closes before calling `on_select` so handler errors, reloads,
      or reentrant menu operations cannot leave stale presentation state.
- [ ] Context-menu presentation may own focus and input while open. It does
      not inherit the tooltip requirement to remain transparent to focus and
      input.
- [ ] Registration may install a reversible, generation-owned wrapper around
      an attached owning Lua screen instance's effective `onInput()` method.
      Hook ownership, restoration, reload invalidation, and foreign-wrapper
      behavior match `dwarfui/tooltip_render_hook.lua`: restore the predecessor
      exactly while DwarfUI remains outermost; if a foreign wrapper is
      outermost, preserve it and leave DwarfUI's superseded trampoline inert
      and diagnosable.
- [ ] Opening hooks only resolve and consume an actionable opening input. While
      the context-menu ZScreen is the current top screen, it is the physical
      input surface for menu interaction and dismissal. If another ZScreen is
      above it, normal DFHack screen-stack routing applies without focus
      trapping, forced raising, or special forwarding.
- [ ] Present the menu as a non-draggable, non-resizable `widgets.Window`
      containing a `widgets.List`, following the DwarfDirect command-menu
      composition. Use the native window frame and title instead of inventing
      separate title or frame interaction.
- [ ] An already-open menu is never replaced by another right-click. A second
      right-click only closes and consumes. Replacement is reserved for a
      future explicit programmatic API and is not part of the initial contract.
- [ ] Classify ownership at the input-table level. If a table contains an
      actionable context-menu input that is handled, dispatch it through the
      native Window/List or service and consume the complete table.
- [ ] While the menu is current, classify event relevance and ownership before
      invoking protected Window/List or service code. Resolve handled events in
      this order: Escape or actionable right-click closes; an actionable
      left-click outside closes; remaining Window/List actions run; an
      otherwise-unhandled left-click inside the complete Window is consumed as
      a no-op. This priority applies even when one table contains several
      relevant keys.
- [ ] Offer wheel input to the List only while the pointer is inside the
      complete Window. A wheel-only table outside the Window is irrelevant and
      is delegated unchanged.
- [ ] If an input table contains no context-menu-relevant input, forward the
      original table unchanged through the appropriate Lua or native parent
      route. Pause and map movement are ordinary examples of pass-through
      events.
- [ ] A down-only input table remains unrelated and transparent in both the
      opening hook and open-menu routing under the Phase 0 seam decision. When
      a down flag is coalesced with an actionable click, consuming the complete
      actionable table also consumes the down flag.
- [ ] A genuine opening miss owns no keys: delegate the original table
      unchanged and preserve the predecessor's exact returns.
- [ ] No implementation or test may rely on loose discriminator strings or
      magic numbers. Closed sets use immutable numeric LuaDoc enums and named
      members.
- [ ] Refactor the shared `dwarfui/pointer` API to expose immutable numeric
      `PointerPolicy` and `PointerResultKind` enums, and migrate all existing
      production consumers and tests from string policies/results in the same
      change.
- [ ] Reload is a destructive development operation for context-menu state. It
      closes the menu, drops every registration and registration identity, and
      requires consumers to register again.
- [ ] No consumer or menu state survives reload. The only permitted
      process-state remainder is minimal hook-chain ownership metadata required
      by the tooltip-style contract to keep an unremovable foreign-wrapped
      trampoline inert and diagnosable.
- [ ] Internal discovery, hook, routing, layout, projection, or rendering
      failures close active presentation, stop owned callback chains, make
      context-menu handling transparent for the rest of the generation, and
      report diagnostics. Consumer `on_select` failures are reported after
      close without disabling the system.
- [ ] Every new or modified class and method has LuaDoc documentation.
- [ ] Local unit evidence, packaged-module evidence, registered live-runtime
      evidence, and manual visual evidence are recorded separately.

## Intended public contract

```lua
local context_menu = reqscript('dwarfui/context_menu/api')

context_menu.register(widget, {
    title='Route stop',
    fg=COLOR_WHITE,
    bg=COLOR_BLACK,
    entries={
        {
            label='Move stop',
            on_select=function(context)
                -- Update the selected stop.
            end,
        },
        {
            label='Delete stop',
            fg=COLOR_LIGHTRED,
            on_select=function(context)
                -- Delete the selected stop.
            end,
        },
    },
})

local handle = context_menu.register_map_tile{
    owner=overlay,
    pos=stop.pos,
    definition=definition,
}
```

The implementation must expose `update(widget, definition)`,
`unregister(widget)`, atomic
`update_map_tile(handle, {pos=pos, definition=definition})`, and
`unregister_map_tile(handle)` operations. `register(widget, definition)` returns
whether it created a new registration; re-registration replaces the definition
and returns false. Update and unregister operations return false for an unknown
widget or handle and true after a successful mutation. Invalid definitions or
positions raise before changing stored state. Callers never mutate a registered
definition table by side effect.

## Planned module layout

```text
src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/
  map_projection.lua
  context_menu/
    api.lua
    definition.lua
    input_hook.lua
    input_sample.lua
    map_target.lua
    registration.lua
    renderer.lua
    root_discovery.lua
    screen.lua
    service.lua
    target_detector.lua
    target.lua
```

The projection decision is frozen: extract `dwarfui/map_projection.lua` and
migrate the existing minecart projection in the same implementation change.
The context-menu adapter, session logic, and focused tests remain inside their
dedicated directories. The separately approved shared pointer enum refactor
modifies `dwarfui/pointer.lua` and its existing consumers; both shared modules
are infrastructure rather than context-menu-owned modules.

## Phase 0 audit record

This audit was completed on 2026-07-30 before adding any context-menu
production module.

### Audited revisions and worktree state

- DwarfUI was audited on branch `context-menu-system`, two commits ahead of
  `origin/context-menu-system`, at
  `028d4fcb7ea6fa1b485b27ff75b38caee7f4a35a`
  (`docs: revise context menu system plan`). The tracked and untracked
  DwarfUI worktree was clean before this planning-document update.
- DFHack source was audited from the detached, tracked-clean
  `53.15-r1` checkout at
  `b12f73a323863761992faf93f15a70a3e8ad2acd`
  (`Changelog and modules for 53.15-r1`). Generated untracked build outputs in
  that checkout are pre-existing and were not used as source evidence.

### Input and ownership seams

- `library/LuaTools.cpp::PushInterfaceKeys()` independently copies
  `_MOUSE_R` from the one-shot `mouse_rbut` flag and `_MOUSE_R_DOWN` from the
  held `mouse_rbut_down` flag. They can therefore appear separately or
  together in one Lua key table. The same relationship holds for `_MOUSE_L`
  and `_MOUSE_L_DOWN`.
- `Lua::Core::Reset()` inhibits a delivered click until the physical button is
  released. There is no later actionable release key in the Lua input table.
  The actionable context-menu boundary is `_MOUSE_R`; a coalesced down flag is
  part of that same table, while a down-only table is held-state observation.
- A focused search of the active DFHack Lua GUI sources found no
  `_MOUSE_R_DOWN` action consumer. `gui.ZScreen`, dialogs, labels, materials,
  and panel context actions use `_MOUSE_R`. `_MOUSE_L_DOWN` is used only for
  continuing drag or text-selection state; List activation and Window drag
  initiation use `_MOUSE_L`. This supports transparent down-only routing
  without a latch or trailing-event suppression.
- `plugins/overlay.cpp` calls
  `plugins.overlay.feed_viewscreen_widgets()` before native viewscreen feed.
  A truthy Lua return skips the native predecessor and calls
  `markInputAsHandled()`; false delegates the original native input. The Lua
  overlay dispatcher likewise stops at the first truthy widget result.
  Context-menu opening must therefore either own the complete table or call
  the prior Lua function once with that same table. Partial reinjection and a
  reentrancy guard would violate this seam.
- `library/modules/Screen.cpp` dynamically resolves the Lua screen's effective
  `onInput` method on every feed and passes one key table. This permits a
  reversible instance-method wrapper. A handled return marks the input
  handled; an opening miss must invoke the captured effective predecessor
  exactly once with the original `self` and table and return all predecessor
  values unchanged.
- The tooltip pointer poller is a one-frame `dfhack.timeout()` sampling chain.
  It observes pointer state after dispatch and has no return path to the
  active input feed. It remains useful precedent for registration-gated
  discovery, but cannot be the opening or consumption seam.
- Event ownership is deliberately table-level. Once Escape, actionable right
  click, outside actionable left click, or a handled Window/List action owns
  the table, every coalesced field is consumed. A miss or irrelevant table is
  passed unchanged; no synthetic remainder is constructed.

### ZScreen, Window, and List behavior

- `gui.ZScreen:render()` renders its parent first, then itself. `hasFocus()`
  requires its native screen to be current. Its default `onInput()` may raise
  a defocused screen under the mouse, dismisses on `LEAVESCREEN` or
  `_MOUSE_R`, and conditionally forwards pause, movement, and mouse input with
  `sendInputToParent()`.
- The context-menu screen will not use that default dispatcher for owned
  input. It will explicitly set `initial_pause=false`, `force_pause=false`,
  `pass_pause=true`, `pass_movement_keys=false`, `pass_mouse_clicks=false`,
  and `defocusable=false`; classify owned tables itself; and delegate complete
  irrelevant tables through `sendInputToParent()`. If another ZScreen becomes
  current, ordinary screen-stack routing applies and the menu neither raises
  itself nor traps focus.
- `widgets.List:onInput()` offers the table to its scrollbar first, then uses
  one `if`/`elseif` chain for `SELECT`, `SELECT_ALL`, `_MOUSE_L`, scrolling,
  choice hotkeys, and label keys. Each successful branch returns, so one intact
  table causes at most one List transition. `_MOUSE_L` selects and immediately
  submits the pointed row. The embedded scrollbar consumes wheel keys only
  while the pointer is within the parent List and uses `_MOUSE_L` for its
  clickable controls.
- Native List painting applies cursor/default/hover pens to rendered label
  fragments, not a guaranteed whole-row background fill. The context-menu
  renderer must paint each complete row with its resolved entry pen before
  using native List input, selection, scrolling, and submission behavior.
- A non-draggable, non-resizable `widgets.Window` delegates to its Panel
  subviews and does not consume an otherwise-unhandled `_MOUSE_L` on its frame
  or empty body. The context-menu screen must preserve any native subview
  handling, then consume such a click inside the complete Window as a no-op.
- DwarfDirect's command menu confirms the intended native composition:
  `widgets.Window` containing `widgets.List`, with
  `gui.FRAME_INTERIOR()` and native submission. Context-menu construction
  additionally disables the Window defaults for dragging and resizing so its
  anchor cannot be mutated by chrome interaction.

### Reused tooltip contracts and deliberate deviations

- Reuse weak, idempotent widget registration; exact integer x/y/z map handles;
  weak map handle/coordinate indexing; atomic map updates; latest-registration
  tie-breaking; exact parent/subview attachment checks; and visible, active,
  enabled, currently presented root eligibility.
- Reuse pointer traversal within each root, widget-over-map precedence, a
  target in any eligible root winning over blockers elsewhere, and blocker
  suppression of map fallback when no widget target wins. Preserve the latest
  original registration sequence for deterministic cross-root selection.
- Reuse the render-hook ownership rule for input wrappers: restore an
  outermost owned wrapper exactly; never overwrite a foreign outer wrapper;
  and leave an unremovable superseded trampoline inert and diagnosable.
- Deliberately do not reuse tooltip registration persistence on reload.
  Context-menu definitions own executable handler closures, so reload closes
  presentation and destructively drops all registrations and session state.
- Opening eligibility uses the strict tooltip root resolver. During an open
  session, the context-menu ZScreen is allowed to sit above the source root:
  validate that the weak source owner remains attached through the menu's
  still-live presented parent/root chain. A later ZScreen above the menu does
  not itself invalidate that chain. Hidden, inactive, detached, disabled, or
  otherwise unpresented owners do invalidate it.

### Projection, enums, colors, and API boundaries

- `dwarfui/minecart_route.lua` contains the authoritative project precedent:
  `Viewport:tileToScreen()` in text mode and Premium viewport-corner,
  `viewport_zoom_factor // 4`, and tile-pixel-to-interface-cell math in
  graphics mode. DFHack 53.15-r1 exposes no public Premium-aware helper with
  the same contract. Extract this math to shared
  `dwarfui/map_projection.lua` and migrate both minecart and context-menu
  consumers atomically.
- Freeze `ContextMenuTargetKind` as `WIDGET=1`, `MAP_TILE=2`;
  `ContextMenuAnchorKind` as `SCREEN_POSITION=1`, `MAP_TILE=2`;
  shared `PointerPolicy` as `TARGET=1`, `PASS=2`, `BLOCK=3`, `NONE=4`; and
  shared `PointerResultKind` as `TARGET=1`, `BLOCKED=2`, `MISS=3`. Production
  code must expose immutable tables and compare named members.
- The pointer-string migration inventory is:
  `dwarfui/pointer.lua`, `dwarfui/tooltip_target_detector.lua`,
  `dwarfui/tooltip.lua`, `dwarfui/widget_extensions.lua`,
  `dwarfui-minecart-route-markers.lua`,
  `tests/infrastructure_smoke.spec.lua`,
  `tests/minecart_route_overlay.spec.lua`,
  `tests/package_contract.spec.lua`, `tests/pointer.spec.lua`,
  `tests/tooltip_registration.spec.lua`, `tests/tooltip_service.spec.lua`,
  `tests/tooltip_target_detector.spec.lua`, `tests/tooltip.spec.lua`, and
  `tests/widget_extensions.spec.lua`.
- The accepted color domain is exactly the integer range
  `COLOR_BLACK..COLOR_WHITE` (`0..15`) from `ColorText.h`. Clone
  `gui.FRAME_INTERIOR()` per menu and apply the resolved menu fg/bg to every
  frame pen, the optional native title, and the otherwise-unpainted Window
  body without mutating shared styles. Paint every entry's complete row with
  its independently resolved fg/bg.
- Target identity and placement are separate session fields. Widget targets
  capture a `SCREEN_POSITION` anchor from the opening pointer; map targets
  retain a copied world coordinate and use a `MAP_TILE` anchor reprojected
  every render.
- The initial public surface is registration-driven only:
  `register`, `update`, `unregister`, `register_map_tile`,
  `update_map_tile`, and `unregister_map_tile`. It exposes neither
  `open_at_*` nor an open-menu replacement operation.

